      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "4.9.4  Backup and Recovery:\nPerform regular database and file backups. \nStore backup files in the approved location. \nVerify successful completion of backups. \nTest recovery procedures at planned intervals. \nMaintain backup and recovery records. \n4.9.5  Portal Data Backup and Storage Allocation:\nThe portal database, uploaded files, system logs, archives and backup copies shall be provided with storage space on the server. The required capacity should be calculated based on the number of users, the transaction volume, the upload frequency, the permitted file size, and the data retention period. Database and application-file backups shall be carried out at defined intervals, with quarterly, half-yearly and yearly copies retained as applicable. At least 25-30% of the free-space shall be maintained for recovery and future growth activities. Backup files will be stored in an approved secure location and periodically verified and reviewed during post-deployment maintenance.\nConsidering a maximum upload size of 100 MB per file, backup storage shall be allocated based on the actual number of uploaded documents, archived files, system records, and the approved retention period. \nFor a portal with approximately 200 uploads per month, a minimum capacity of 400 GB per year shall be provided. Where quarterly full backups are retained, approximately 1 TB of dedicated backup storage shall be allocated and reviewed periodically based on actual data growth. \n",
